Mother's Day in Tears<i>!</i>

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:09.600
Mother's Day in Tears<i>!</i>

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.460
Good afternoon.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:12.790
Good afternoon!

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:13.980
Welcome!

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.610
Yo, Nami, Rumi!

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:18.090
I'd like some carrots and potatoes, please.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.190
Thank you! That'll be 250 yen.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.560
We've got a fantastic bargain on tomatoes today too!

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:24.160
Only 100 yen for three!

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.030
Then I'll take those too! How about 300 yen for the lot?

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.680
300 yen for the lot!

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.840
I can't beat you two, can I, Nami?

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:33.290
Go on, I'll throw 'em in for free.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:34.930
Yay!

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:39.860
Let's see... I didn't forget to get anything, did I?

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.260
Hey, Mommy?

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.060
What was this flower called again?

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.640
Well, that flower is called a "carnation."

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.060
It's really pretty!

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.210
Rumi?

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:54.390
Sis! I want a carnation too!

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:55.600
Huh?

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:01.130
Still, it's impressive just how many carnations you've got out here.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.570
Things like roses and gerberas are selling all right,

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:06.780
but carnations are definitely the most popular at the moment.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.310
Good afternoon.

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:09.490
Good afternoon!

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.120
Naminami!

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:15.720
It seems everyone at the nursery said they wanted to give their mothers carnations,

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:17.580
so Rumi wants to as well.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.630
Although in our case it's more of an offering.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:23.010
Well, it's the sentiment that's important.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:27.680
I think working so hard to decide what to pick is just as important as the gift itself.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:32.510
I'm still not sure what to get for my mom either.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:35.070
Every year I get her a handkerchief or an apron or something...

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:38.480
She's always grateful, but it's kinda getting predictable.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:39.690
Same here.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:43.160
I know it's the thought that counts, but...

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:47.240
Well then, why not try buying Mother's Day presents for each other?

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.180
Huh?

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.320
Then you'll have a different 
present from usual, won't you?

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.540
I see!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.270
That's a nice idea! {"nice idea" in English}

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.700
I-I'm so sorry!

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:00.790
I really shouldn't be asking you about Mother's Day, Shiku...

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:05.700
